-- 657_holiday_corridor_seed_repair.sql — fall + Halloween SOLO seeds that stage the person on a route get a spot to
-- stand at instead, same place and theme (2026-10-02).
--
-- Kevin flagged three nightlies from 2026-10-02 (sunnysteph, tiffany, michele) that all looked like "a woman walking
-- forward on a path with fall scenery". Measured: 7 of 19 holiday solos since 2026-09-26 were that shot (women 6/9)
-- against 2 of 20 non-holiday solos. The solo prompt's early "set at" line is the seed's first comma-clause, and
-- flux-1.1-pro stages the person on whatever it names; a route there (avenue, trail, rows, aisle, dock, covered-bridge
-- deck) renders the person centred on it with the route receding behind. Same-seed probe on the production prompts
-- (scratchpad, flux-1.1-pro, 6 seeds each): shipped seed 20/24 corridor shots; the same place led by a spot 2/24, and
-- the Halloween props the seed named came back (0/6 -> 6/6).
--
--   A. 410 rows a judge read flagged as route-staged (scripts/fix-holiday-corridor-seeds.js): rewritten so the first
--      clause names a spot in the same place (a bench under the maples, the side rail of the covered bridge, a hay bale
--      in the corn maze clearing); a route that IS the theme stays once, after the first clause, as "beside the ...".
--   B. 68 rows the judge passed that still named a route mid-seed (the porch seed "jack-o-lanterns creating a luminous
--      path" rendered the corridor in production): only that phrase reworded (--light); vineyards lead with their
--      fountain, barrels or press.
-- Every rewrite read by hand; 26 edited by hand (copied example phrases, spots inside a covered bridge, a dropped
-- vineyard). Couples (dual_scenarios) untouched.
--
-- Every statement is guarded (still the old text), so a re-run changes nothing.
-- ROLLBACK: swap each statement's SET and WHERE text (scripts/fix-holiday-corridor-seeds.js --from <rewrites.json>
-- --sql <file> --rollback writes it).

-- A. route-staged rows (410)
